  "body": "Given that a large number of apps use innerHTML to construct the DOM, and that a lot lead to taking strings that are fairly large and that come from servers, would it make sense to make innerHTML take something that is ```Streamable``` so that it can take things incrementally rather than synchronously? Any chance that could take things off of the main thread?\r\n\r\n(filling retroactively from a discussion with @slightlyoff)",
